{
 "title": "Image textures: a PBR set",
 "summary": "Image textures and PBR maps. The tutor downloads a brick set (colour, normal, roughness, displacement, AO); here Lucius bakes its own from a procedural brick material with Cycles into the same five images. Then the tutor's steps: an Image Texture with the colour image on Object coordinates, fixed on the sides with Box projection; the better way through UV coordinates and UVs scaled so the image fills each face; the normal map (Non-Color) through a Normal Map node; roughness (Non-Color); the displacement into a Bump node (strength 0.5) fed by the normal map; the AO map as the factor of a Mix Color for coloured (blue) fake shadows. Beyond the tutorial: a wall with the full set tiled by scaling its UVs.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "BoxProjected",
   "description": ""
  },
  {
   "name": "ColorOnly",
   "description": ""
  },
  {
   "name": "NormalMapped",
   "description": ""
  },
  {
   "name": "FullPBR",
   "description": ""
  },
  {
   "name": "BlueShadows",
   "description": ""
  },
  {
   "name": "BrickBackdrop",
   "description": ""
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "Five brick cubes in front of a tiled brick wall: box-projected, flat colour, normal-mapped, full PBR with relief, and one with blue shadows in the joints.",
